WEBVTT

00:11:27.455 --> 00:11:30.486
and for assessing leadership
and interpersonal skills.

00:11:30.510 --> 00:11:31.957
LR: The scenario is based on,

00:11:31.981 --> 00:11:33.863
"This is the kind of stuff we do here,

00:11:33.887 --> 00:11:35.864
and let's see how you would approach it."

00:11:35.888 --> 00:11:38.087
AG: I also like including
situational questions

00:11:38.111 --> 00:11:41.503
because they level the playing field
for candidates with less experience

00:11:41.527 --> 00:11:44.345
who might not have relevant stories
to tell from their past.

00:11:44.369 --> 00:11:46.608
You get to see how they
approach the challenges

00:11:46.632 --> 00:11:49.629
that are unique to the job
and to your organization.

00:11:49.653 --> 00:11:51.234
You can even create an answer key

00:11:51.258 --> 00:11:54.178
by giving the questions to a bunch
of your existing employees,

00:11:54.202 --> 00:11:57.218
and seeing how the star performers
respond differently.

00:11:57.242 --> 00:12:00.253
Basically, structured
interviews get you better data,